```

Repository methods:
- `insert(Suspension)` → id
- `findActive(long incidentId)` → Optional<Suspension> (resumed_at IS NULL)
- `listByIncident(long incidentId)` → List ordered by id
- `resume(long id, String resumedBy, String resumeNote, Instant resumedAt)` → int (conditional `AND resumed_at IS NULL`)
- `findById`? After resume, re-fetch via findActive won't work. Re-fetch by id: `findById(long id)`.

Service methods:

```java
@Transactional
public SuspensionView suspend(String incidentKey, String actor, SuspendRequest req) {
    String commandKey = requireText(req.commandKey(), "commandKey");
    String suspendKey = requireText(req.suspendKey(), "suspendKey");
    String reason = requireText(req.reason(), "reason");
    Incident incident = lockIncident(incidentKey);
    return runIdempotent(commandKey, "suspend", hash(incidentKey, actor, suspendKey, reason),
            SuspensionView.class, () -> {
                requireCommander(incident, actor);
                requireSuspendable(incident);
                if (suspensions.findActive(incident.id()).isPresent()) {
                    throw ApiException.conflict("已存在生效挂起，不能重复挂起");
                }
                long limitSeconds = CONTAINMENT_MINUTES.get(incident.severity()) * 60;
                long accumulated = closedSuspensionSeconds(incident.id());
                if (accumulated >= limitSeconds) {
                    throw ApiException.suspensionLimit("累计挂起时长已达上限: 已累计 " + accumulated + " 秒, 上限 " + limitSeconds + " 秒");
                }
                Instant now = now();
                long id = suspensions.insert(new Suspension(0L, incident.id(), suspendKey, reason, actor, now, null, null, null, now));
                return toSuspensionView(suspensions.findById(id).orElseThrow());
            });
}
```

requireSuspendable: status must be COMMANDING (else 409 "已遏制/已关闭/未接管事件不能挂起"), and escalation ACKNOWLEDGED → 409.

Wait: for REPORTED, commander is null so requireCommander already throws 409. Good. For CONTAINED/RESOLVED/CLOSED, commander exists, so need explicit status check. And ACKNOWLEDGED escalation check.

```java
private void requireSuspendable(Incident incident) {
    if (incident.status() != IncidentStatus.COMMANDING) {
        throw ApiException.conflict(incident.status() + " 状态不允许挂起遏制时限");
    }
    var esc = escalations.findByIncident(incident.id());
    if (esc.isPresent() && esc.get().status() == EscalationStatus.ACKNOWLEDGED) {
        throw ApiException.conflict("升级已确认的事件不能挂起遏制时限");
    }
}
```

Resume:
```java
@Transactional
public SuspensionView resume(String incidentKey, String actor, ResumeRequest req) {
    String commandKey = requireText(req.commandKey(), "commandKey");
    String suspendKey = requireText(req.suspendKey(), "suspendKey");
    String note = requireText(req.note(), "note");
    Incident incident = lockIncident(incidentKey);
    return runIdempotent(commandKey, "resume", hash(incidentKey, actor, suspendKey, note),
            SuspensionView.class, () -> {
                requireCommander(incident, actor);
                Suspension active = suspensions.findActive(incident.id())
                        .orElseThrow(() -> ApiException.conflict("当前没有生效挂起，不能恢复"));
                if (!active.suspendKey().equals(suspendKey)) {
                    throw ApiException.conflict("suspendKey 与生效挂起不匹配: " + suspendKey);
                }
                Instant now = now();
                suspensions.resume(active.id(), actor, note, now);
                return toSuspensionView(suspensions.findById(active.id()).orElseThrow());
            });
}
```

Does resume require commander? "恢复须提交同一 suspendKey 与说明" — doesn't explicitly say commander, but consistency suggests commander. Hmm. During suspension a transfer could occur... then new commander resumes. Requiring current commander is reasonable. I'll require commander (409 otherwise), consistent with all other write ops.

