}
```

Use millis or seconds? Timestamps are microsecond precision. Use Duration and expose remainingSeconds as long seconds. Duration.between(...).toSeconds() truncates. For tests, use whole seconds. I'll compute with Duration and use `.toSeconds()` — but negative durations? Not possible since resumedAt >= suspendedAt and now >= suspendedAt for active (clock could go backwards in tests but won't).

Effective deadline = deadlineAt + suspendedTotal. remaining = Duration.between(now, effectiveDeadline).toSeconds() clamped to >= 0. overdue = now >= effectiveDeadline (i.e., !now.isBefore(eff)).

